new file mode 100644
index 0000000..d76da37
--- /dev/null
+++ b/SOLUTION.md
@@ -0,0 +1,15 @@
+# Solution
+
+Two bugs in `lrucache/cache.py`:
+
+1. **`get()` did not refresh recency.** On a cache hit it returned the value
+   without calling `move_to_end(key)`, so reads never counted as "use". A key
+   that had just been read could still be evicted as the least-recently-used
+   entry. Fixed by moving the key to the end of the `OrderedDict` on every
+   non-expired hit.
+
+2. **`put()` evicted on updates of existing keys.** It evicted whenever
+   `len(self._data) >= capacity`, even when the incoming key was already
+   present and was only being overwritten — so updating a key in a full cache
+   wrongly dropped an unrelated entry. Fixed by only evicting when the key is
+   new (`key not in self._data`) and the cache is at capacity.
